{
 "_what_this_is": "Settings of the metal reuse trial (metal_recipe.py reads this). Every shared layer is unchanged; only these numbers differ from slate. MOSS paints rust, DAMAGE paints chipped paint. Colours from the metal reference's measured 8- and 12-colour palettes, sizes from its measured summary numbers; then tuned by hand by eye. Second round (by the second helper): diagonal braces were added to the new metal layout (the metal_layout.brace_* settings), and the rust, speckle, grain and chip settings were tuned again by hand on seed set 1 (rounds 5 and 6: rounder rust, finer speckle, more chips, then more contrast). Round 7: after the first final bake showed 31 and 34 percent rust on seed sets 2 and 3 (22 on set 1, the reference has 22), the rust was made less patchy and a little less in all (moss.patchiness, patch_size, coverage) and the sun-bleach a little weaker; the final tiles were baked again.",

